### Typography

Establish consistent sizes and spacing.

- Page title: approximately 30–34px
- Section heading: 20–24px
- Account heading: 16–18px
- Standard body: 14–16px
- Supporting information: 13–14px
- Metadata: approximately 12px

Use professional sans-serif typography.

Use tabular numerals for metrics, financial values, and dates.

Avoid excessive uppercase text and decorative miniature labels.

### Layout

Create a shared desktop layout with:

- Approximately 248px primary sidebar
- Approximately 64px stable top toolbar
- Disciplined 12-column content grid
- Appropriate content maximum width
- Consistent 4px/8px spacing system
- Predictable panel, table, and control spacing
- Purposeful contextual drawers

Adapt intelligently to mobile and tablet sizes.

### Visual discipline

Do not rely on oversized KPI cards, repetitive rectangular tiles, excessive gradients, glowing components, unnecessary shadows, decorative charts, or multiple competing primary colors.

Use information rows, structured tables, meaningful timelines, carefully selected emphasis, and subtle visual separators.

**The interface should communicate importance through hierarchy, not decoration.**

